From: goldenvess3g project (derived from Google android-3.4 kernel/common, drivers/staging/android/binder.c)
Subject: [PROPOSAL, applied only to experimental kernel copies] binder: call the five LSM hooks

Adds the five security_binder_* calls that SELinux's binder class needs, at the same places as Google's
android-3.4 branch: set_context_mgr, transaction (before the one-way/reply stack logic), transfer_binder (BINDER and
HANDLE objects) and transfer_file (with fput and the existing error label). Nothing else from Google's binder.c is taken
(it also differs in unrelated fixes; see docs/phase-8-selinux-runtime-validation.md).

